OL,3,GNEWSAMore than one in three children
OL,4,Aliving in poverty
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than a third of children in the
OL,7,FWest Midlands are living in poverty,
OL,8,Fnew data has revealed.
OL,10,FAcross Birmingham, Coventry, Dudley,
OL,11,FSandwell, Solihull, Walsall and
OL,12,FWolverhampton, 36% of children are
OL,13,Faffected by deprivation, with it rising
OL,14,Fto 62% in the Ladywood area of
OL,15,FBirmingham.
OL,17,FThe data was revealed in the West
OL,18,FMidlands State of the Region 2026
OL,19,Fannual review, which was presented to
OL,20,Fthe West Midlands Combined Authority's
OL,21,F(WMCA) Local Scrutiny Committee.
OL,23,APub: 02-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,360,350,200,160,0,100
